;; Named refusals for remotes the compiled service namespaces mention but the
;; native image cannot honour (host-compiler.scm: native-service-refusals).
;; This file loads LAST: a key that any host file provides keeps that provider.
(for-each (lambda (key)
  (if (not (native-map-has? native-leaf-registry key))
   (begin (set! native-excluded-host-leaves (cons key native-excluded-host-leaves))
          (native-add-leaf! key (native-unavailable key)))))
 native-service-refusals)
;; N0: remotes the native front end's own units name (host/record.bl, host/aot.bl
;; and front-end/stage.bl as image units, front-end/n0/compose.py) that no host
;; file provides. Evaluated, they failed at their call; compiled, the linker
;; needs a target for each, so each is a named refusal that fails the same way
;; at its call, and function_exported answers false as before. A host leaf or
;; nf-route! for a key replaces its refusal. Listed by front-end/n0/remotes.bl.
;; The first two are named by main's boot units, which postdate chez-main
;; (core's all-ns, find-ns and require's guesses; the compiler's ns_home); the
